          "statedBy": "a restock in one warehouse raises the storefront number live"
        }
      ],
      "note": "The rush assertion only means something if a restock works at all, so the control runs first and has to move the number. Without it a restock that never reached the server and a restock lost to a race look identical: both leave stock at start - purchases. The control also separates the two, by reading what the server stored (admin-location-qty) before what the buyer sees (item-stock). Totals are asserted as CHANGES rather than absolute values, because earlier features buy from the same catalogue."
