        {
          "id": "203b",
          "desc": "checking the same cart out twice at once produces one order",
          "points": 1,
          "steps": [
            {
              "do": "click",
              "actor": "tab1",
              "testid": "checkout-submit"
            },
            {
              "do": "wait",
              "actor": "tab1",
              "ms": 2500
            },
            {
              "do": "fill",
              "actor": "tab2",
              "testid": "search-input",
              "text": "Webcam",
              "enter": true,
              "settleMs": 1500
            },
            {
              "do": "click",
              "actor": "tab2",
              "testid": "add-to-cart",
              "in": {
                "testid": "item-card",
                "contains": "Webcam"
              }
            },
            {
              "do": "wait",
              "actor": "tab2",
              "ms": 1200
            },
            {
              "do": "click",
              "actor": "tab2",
              "testid": "cart-toggle"
            },
            {
              "do": "click",
              "actor": "tab2",
              "testid": "checkout-submit"
            },
            {
              "do": "wait",
              "actor": "tab2",
              "ms": 2500
            },
            {
              "do": "fill",
              "actor": "filler",
              "testid": "search-input",
              "text": "Keyboard",
              "enter": true,
              "settleMs": 1500
            },
            {
              "do": "click",
              "actor": "filler",
              "testid": "add-to-cart",
              "in": {
                "testid": "item-card",
                "contains": "Keyboard"
              }
            },
            {
              "do": "wait",
              "actor": "filler",
              "ms": 2000
            },
            {
              "do": "callConcurrently",
              "actors": [
                "tab1",
                "tab2"
              ],
              "action": "checkout",
              "settleMs": 5000
            },
            {
              "do": "expectCallOutcomes",
              "accepted": 1
            },
            {
              "do": "click",
              "actor": "filler",
              "testid": "orders-toggle"
            },
            {
              "do": "expect",
              "actor": "filler",
              "testid": "order-item",
              "contains": "Keyboard",
              "count": 1
            }
          ],
          "note": "replayConcurrently replays each actor's LAST POST, so a racing tab must not touch the cart after its checkout is captured — that would overwrite the captured request with an add-to-cart. A third session on the same account fills the cart instead, leaving tab1 and tab2 holding nothing but their checkouts. A checkout carries no JSON body, so it never lands in lastWrites — the replay must select it by URL with the match option, or it silently races the last add-to-cart instead.",
          "provenBy": "checkout-not-idempotent (postgres-ecom-l1.json): stripping FOR UPDATE from the cart read at checkout made two replayed checkout requests each create an order — the criterion failed on its own assertion (expected exactly 1 order containing Keyboard, found 2). The unmutated app passes, refusing the second checkout with a 400.",
          "withheld": "uses the spec's named `checkout` action so it can be issued on either stack. It previously replayed a captured HTTP write, which SpacetimeDB never produces — that client writes over WebSocket — so the criterion reported INCONCLUSIVE there and the two backends were scored out of different totals. Points retained: it has already failed a mutant on the stacks that could run it.",
          "statedBy": "checking out twice must not produce two orders"
        }
      ],
      "note": "Both tabs reach the item by search rather than trusting the storefront: earlier features in this suite buy things, which re-ranks the top ten. Each tab opens its OWN cart — panel state belongs to a browser context, not to the feature."
    }
